ZERO NETWORK AND BROWSER TRANSPORT ABI 0.13

Original Zero implementation. The existing computation worker2 runs a bounded
network poll before yielding. Locals are private. console remains constant;
work is the network base. The parent always schedules worker2, so pause3 does
not suspend DHCP/recovery. Network operations never write user disk sectors.

Memory ownership
console+2400: network state pointer, or0 when no safe DMA region exists.
console+2408: WiFi UI/radio state pointer = network+24576.
Network/browser reserve pool+163840 through pool+393216 (229376 bytes).
Wired control/DMA own offsets0..24575; WiFi owns24576..32767.
Raw response owns32768..98303; decoded body owns98304..163839.
Browser state owns163840..229375. Window slots begin at pool+393216.
Pool minimum532480; usable window capacity is (poolsize-524288)/8192.
Initialization zeroes the complete reserved region and rejects a misaligned,
overflowed, too-small or above4GiB DMA pool. Compiler workspace is separate.

